## Case: py-dispatch-dual-len
id: "av.parity.1094.py-dispatch-dual-len"
tags: ["av-language-parity", "plan-1094"]
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "main.as"
syntax: "auto-script"

```auto
use.py numpy: arange
fn main() int {
 var t = arange(6)
 print(t.len())
 var s = "abc"
 print(s.len())
 return 0
}
```

### Probe av
recipe: "ac-av/language-source-run-v1"
entry: "d_main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1", "foreign.scalar", "foreign.resource", "console.stdout", "console.stderr"]
foreign: { kind: "rust", provider: "py" }
exit: 0

#### stdout

```text
6
3
```

#### stderr

```text
```

### Notes

Legacy 99_py_dispatch/01_dual_len: `.len()` on a Python object is the
`__len__` protocol (the numpy array's first axis, 6); a native Auto `str`
keeps its scalar count (3). Requires the numpy interpreter module.

## Case: native-len-unchanged
id: "av.parity.1094.native-len-unchanged"
tags: ["av-language-parity", "plan-1094"]
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "main.at"

```auto
fn main() int {
 var s = "abcdef"
 if s.len() != 6 { return 0 }
 var xs = [1, 2, 3, 4]
 if xs.len() != 4 { return 0 }
 var t = "x" + s
 if t.len() != 7 { return 0 }
 return 42
}
```

### Probe av
recipe: "ac-av/language-source-run-v1"
entry: "d_main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1", "console.stdout", "console.stderr"]
exit: 42

#### stdout

```text
```

#### stderr

```text
```

### Notes

Legacy 99_py_dispatch/02_auto_str_unchanged: pure Auto values (str / List)
keep their native `.len()` semantics — no py dispatch, no adapter load.

