## Case: with-error-message
id: "av.parity.1094.with-error-message"
tags: ["av-language-parity", "plan-1094"]
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "main.as"
syntax: "auto-script"

```auto
use.py io: StringIO
use.py contextlib: closing
use.py builtins: int
fn main() int {
 let buf = StringIO()
 try {
  with closing(buf) as r {
   r.write("ok")
   var boom = int("xyz")
  }
 } catch e { print("caught: " + e.to(str)) }
 print("end")
 return 0
}
```

### Probe av
recipe: "ac-av/language-source-run-v1"
entry: "d_main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1", "foreign.scalar", "foreign.resource", "console.stdout", "console.stderr"]
foreign: { kind: "rust", provider: "py" }
exit: 0

#### stdout

```text
caught: PyException ValueError: invalid literal for int() with base 10: 'xyz'
end
```

#### stderr

```text
```

### Notes

Legacy 99_script_err/04_with_as_propagate: a Python error raised INSIDE a
`with` body runs `__exit__` exactly once and propagates to the outer catch —
the with exit obligations hold for error exits.

## Case: py-object-not-callable
id: "av.parity.1094.py-object-not-callable"
tags: ["av-language-parity", "plan-1094"]
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "main.as"
syntax: "auto-script"

```auto
use.py builtins: int
fn main() int {
 var a = int(42)
 try { var b = a(1) } catch e { print("caught: " + e.to(str)) }
 return 0
}
```

### Probe av
recipe: "ac-av/language-source-run-v1"
entry: "d_main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1", "foreign.scalar", "foreign.resource", "console.stdout", "console.stderr"]
foreign: { kind: "rust", provider: "py" }
exit: 0

#### stdout

```text
caught: PyException TypeError: 'int' object is not callable
```

#### stderr

```text
```

### Notes

Legacy 99_script_err/05_obj_call_auto_catch: a REAL Python `TypeError`
(class 3) is catchable. The legacy's conservative obj_call FALSE POSITIVE on
Auto values (`.upper()` mis-routed) is NOT replicated — a native `str`'s
methods route natively (the plan's named decision, "旧 obj_call Auto 分支假
阳性等 bug 不机械复制").

## Case: with-break-exits-once
id: "av.parity.1094.with-break-exits-once"
tags: ["av-language-parity", "plan-1094"]
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "main.as"
syntax: "auto-script"

```auto
use.py io: StringIO
use.py contextlib: closing
fn main() int {
 let buf = StringIO()
 var i = 0
 for i < 3 {
  with closing(buf) as r { r.write("ok"); break }
 }
 if buf.closed.to(bool) { return 42 }; return 0
}
```

### Probe av
recipe: "ac-av/language-source-run-v1"
entry: "d_main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1", "foreign.scalar", "foreign.resource", "console.stdout", "console.stderr"]
foreign: { kind: "rust", provider: "py" }
exit: 42

#### stdout

```text
```

#### stderr

```text
```

### Notes

WITH-EXITS (break): `break` inside a `with` body routes through `__exit__`
EXACTLY ONCE (buf.closed proves the exit ran), then the loop exits.

## Case: with-nested-exits
id: "av.parity.1094.with-nested-exits"
tags: ["av-language-parity", "plan-1094"]
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "main.as"
syntax: "auto-script"

```auto
use.py io: StringIO
use.py contextlib: closing
fn main() int {
 let buf1 = StringIO()
 let buf2 = StringIO()
 with closing(buf1) as a {
  with closing(buf2) as b { b.write("x") }
 }
 if buf1.closed.to(bool) && buf2.closed.to(bool) { return 42 }; return 0
}
```

### Probe av
recipe: "ac-av/language-source-run-v1"
entry: "d_main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1", "foreign.scalar", "foreign.resource", "console.stdout", "console.stderr"]
foreign: { kind: "rust", provider: "py" }
exit: 42

#### stdout

```text
```

#### stderr

```text
```

### Notes

WITH-EXITS (nested): nested `with` blocks both run their `__exit__` in
Python's LIFO order (both buffers closed).
